    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d994">

                <pb facs="1162" n="1052" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1052"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.79611 Pangborn-Herndon Flight/117</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Chief of the Division of
                        Far Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">of a Conversation With the Japanese Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kato</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-28">August 28, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Kato telephoned and informed Mr. Hamilton that after Mr. Castle’s talk with
                    the Japanese Ambassador on August 27, the Ambassador had sent a further telegram
                    to the Japanese Foreign Office requesting that favorable action be taken by the
                    Japanese authorities in reference to the issuance of the permit to Messrs.
                    Pangborn and Herndon to fly from Japan.</p>
                <p>Mr. Hamilton thanked Mr. Kato for this information and expressed appreciation of
                    the action taken by the Japanese Embassy.</p>
                <closer><signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
